{
  "action": "After a standard system update you need to restart any running Java\napplications to make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-60589",
    "CVE-2026-70907",
    "CVE-2026-61308"
  ],
  "description": "Kai Aizen discovered that the Networking component of OpenJDK 17 did not\ncorrectly handle user authentication. A remote attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to leak sensitive information. (CVE-2026-61308)\n\nIt was discovered that the JSSE component of OpenJDK 17 did not correctly\nhandle user authentication. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service. (CVE-2026-70907)\n\nIt was discovered that the Security component of OpenJDK 17 did not\ncorrectly handle user authentication. A remote attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to leak sensitive information. (CVE-2026-60589)",
  "id": "USN-8795-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in OpenJDK 17.",
